      "writtenOn": "2024-06-20T06:03:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this is set and the caller is trying to use something other than TETHERING_VIRTUAL, then the code will not use the passed-in interface.\n\nWe should notify the developer that what they are trying to do will not work. Either we throw an exception (UnsupportedOperationException?) when the developer calls TetheringRequest.Builder#build, or we define a new TETHER_ERROR_xxx value and add that value to the StartTetheringError @IntDef.\n\nHaving build() throw is probably easiest. It\u0027s also appropriate because it\u0027s a programming error, rather than an exceptional condition - it will never succeed. We should document that in the javadoc of setInterfaceName.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 706,
        "startChar": 67,
        "endLine": 706,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "37734f7fe2f96efe130c064072a0191e73e6125d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
